      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The recurring of abdominal pain can be a taxing clinical ordeal for the primary care physician or consultant. It often is a test of stamina, of diagnostic self-confidence, of fiscal constraint, and of vigilance for rare conditions. The clinician is apt to be haunted by the lingering question: \"Am I missing something?\" That which might or might not be \"missed\" comprises the content as well as the rationale for this review."},
